FinePrint — agent coordination log
==================================

Append-only. Newest entry at the BOTTOM. Never edit or delete an earlier entry;
correct it with a new one that says what changed.

The LAST entry is the current state. Read it before you start: its ACTIVE line
says what is claimed and NEXT says what to pick up. There is no shared "current
status" block on purpose — a single append per agent cannot conflict with
another agent's append the way a shared block would.

ENTRY FORMAT
------------
### <ISO date> · <nnn> · <short title>
AGENT     who did it (model / session, or a human name)
STATE     done | in-progress | blocked | handoff
TOUCHED   files created or modified
VERIFY    the command that proves it, and its result
SUMMARY   what changed and why, in a few lines
ACTIVE    files you are still holding, or "none"
NEXT      the single most useful thing to do next
NOTES     gotchas the next agent would otherwise rediscover (optional)

Rules: claim files in ACTIVE before a long edit. If your STATE is
"in-progress" or "blocked", say so plainly — a silent stall costs more than an
admitted one. Entries 001–007 were reconstructed at the end of the first
session, so their timestamps are approximate; everything after is written live.


