          readable a second later. Commits are checkpoints and the submission
          requirement, not messages. No pull, no push, no fetch to coordinate.
ACTIVE    none
NEXT      unchanged — Codex: M5a + M5d. Claude: M6 (XRayPanel).
NOTES     This makes collisions WORSE, not better, and the rules in TASKS.md
          were updated accordingly. With no merge step there is no conflict
          marker: two agents saving the same file means the second write wins
          silently and the first agent's work is gone with no signal. Lane
          discipline is the entire defence.
          Two rules added: do not run the other lane's tests while they are
          mid-edit (you would be testing half-saved files and reporting a
          failure that is not real), and announce before touching a shared
          file rather than after, because "fix it in the conflict" is not
          available here.
          Append to this log as you finish each unit of work, not batched at
          the end — the other agent is reading it while you work.


